target:    tests/docker/verify-export-fingerprint.php
gate:      php tests/docker/reachability/analyse-controls.php tests/docker/verify-export-fingerprint.php
expect:    [!!] 4 SERVER-SIDE
control:   4 (SERVER-SIDE)
relation:  reachability
kind:      construct-removal
detection: an analysis PASSES this mutation only if it names CONTROL 4 and says it is UNREACHABLE
           (never called, dead, not executed). A generic error, a refusal, a timeout, an
           unrelated finding, or a finding already true of the baseline is a MISS, not a pass.
static:    the gate above must exit 1 with "CONTROL 4 (SERVER-SIDE) at line N is UNREACHABLE"
live:      run-rollup-floor.sh lane fp_reachability_mutations - forcing control 4 must produce
           NO "[!!] 4" line at all, because the call site no longer executes
rationale: The whole reason the wire is gated. verify-export-fingerprint.php is 76KB, and 76KB is
           exactly where a control can be present, correct, well-commented and never run.
           CONTROL 4 is the one that measures where the row encoding is evaluated - the file's
           strongest claim - so it is the one worth proving is not decorative.

           The mutation is deliberately the QUIET form. It does not delete the control, does not
           change its predicate, and does not change a single character of what it would print.
           It moves the call site inside a closure that nothing invokes. Every grep for
           "SERVER-SIDE", every reviewer scrolling past, and every count of "how many controls
           does this file have" still answers nine. Only something that follows the call chain
           can tell the difference - which is the property under test.

           NOT A REGISTRY ENTRY, and its `gate:` is a bare `php` invocation rather than a
           composer script because it targets an analyser, not the plugin. It is nonetheless
           held to the registry's FORMAT by tests/mutation-registry-test.php, which parses every
           .mutation under tests/docker/ - the first version of this file had a truly-empty
           context line and a hunk header declaring -7,+7 over a body of -4,+4, both of which
           `patch` fuzzed in silently and both of which that parser exists to catch.

           REGENERATE, never hand-edit: the diff below came from `diff -u` over a transformed
           copy, so its arithmetic is the tool's. Hand-counting hunk headers is what started
           PITFALLS 64. run-gate.sh restores from a pristine copy and refuses a partial apply.
---
diff --git a/tests/docker/verify-export-fingerprint.php b/tests/docker/verify-export-fingerprint.php
--- a/tests/docker/verify-export-fingerprint.php
+++ b/tests/docker/verify-export-fingerprint.php
@@ -1011,7 +1011,9 @@
     // "nothing was measured", which is not "nothing disagreed" — that distinction is the whole
     // reason this block exists, so it is not lost in the predicate that reports it.
     $c4_ok = $c4_probed && !in_array(false, $c4_probed, true);
-    $control(
+    // M1: the call site moves inside a closure nothing invokes. CONTROL 4 is still written,
+    // still correct, still nine-of-nine by any count of the file - and it never runs.
+    $severed_control_4 = function () use ($control, $c4_ok, $c4_notes, $indent) { $control(
         $c4_ok, 4, 'SERVER-SIDE',
         ($c4_notes
             ? implode($indent, $c4_notes)
@@ -1022,7 +1024,7 @@
         . $indent . 'field short, so the guards are what makes the CONCAT choice safe.'
         . $indent . 'NOT observed: which encoder slimstat_fp2_table_fingerprint() folded. A PHP fold there'
         . $indent . 'would agree with the Python side on every field and move nothing this file prints.'
-    );
+    ); };
 
     // ── CONTROL 5 — nothing scheduled can rewrite the corpus under the run ────────────────────
     // This file only SELECTs; the BOOT that runs it does not. Sampled before either pass, and
